0-5ecf-abe4-4ef195040d31" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=2,$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it is one-to-one on that interval.\n\nThe function is constant: distinct inputs in each listed interval have the same output $2$. Thus it is not one-to-one on any of the three intervals.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of these intervals\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513203 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "822ed65c-479c-5147-9dc8-b41dd3fd0810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513210} {:answer/id #uuid "cb2f7804-b38c-5fdc-9e4a-2633c4a5d087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513227}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "822ed65c-479c-5147-9dc8-b41dd3fd0810" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513210} :answer-field/id #uuid "b5a5f4e4-cfa4-5892-ad1b-880a9fe20d4d" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513220} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35724131-51b1-5650-8379-cd697029ec72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513197} {:answer/id #uuid "b9ec01b4-8855-5eed-8d35-2e0b3a9270d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35724131-51b1-5650-8379-cd697029ec72" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513197} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd93f924-7b0e-587d-a3b9-eb939063d9a7" :answer-field/key "$x\\in (0,1]$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513223} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f1fed61-97ad-5ade-aae2-213abe68defb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513187} {:answer/id #uuid "e8a584cd-4a11-57a0-97eb-a24cd1c40205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513236}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e8a584cd-4a11-57a0-97eb-a24cd1c40205" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513236} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3a0f93f-1a9a-5ff5-9861-3ecab65a85cd" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-1,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513234}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "64c7ad19-8343-5b7b-a647-af679630a146" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=(x-\\frac{1}{2})^{2},$ on which of the following intervals is $f(x)$ invertible?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "A function is invertible on a particular interval if and only if it is one-to-one on that interval.\n\nThe vertex occurs at $x=\\frac{1}{2}$. On either side of this vertex, the function is strictly monotone. Including the vertex as an endpoint does not create a repeated output. An interval containing points on both sides is not one-to-one: inputs equally far from the vertex have the same output.\n\n- Interval $x\\in [-1,0)$, $[-1,0)$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $0\\le \\frac{1}{2}$. It is therefore invertible.\n\n- Interval $x\\in (\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]$, $(\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $\\frac{1}{2}\\ge \\frac{1}{2}$. It is therefore invertible.\n\n- Interval $x\\in (0,1]$, $(0,1]$, contains the distinct inputs $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\frac{3}{4}$, both with output $\\frac{1}{16}$. It is therefore not invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-1,0)$; $x\\in (\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513209 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a9e7e29d-dc45-5fb6-bcfc-e630b22d851e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513214} {:answer/id #uuid "d6fdd4d7-c2bc-5448-a362-fdc0305229e4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513230}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9e7e29d-dc45-5fb6-bcfc-e630b22d851e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513214} :answer-field/id #uuid "1609602e-0674-5732-94d2-5a4eb6787ad8" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [- \\frac{1}{2},\\frac{1}{2})$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513185} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "337093dc-4523-5eef-afd3-5293321cae5b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513196} {:answer/id #uuid "b38c6770-6eda-5a89-ab2a-58cf95d1000e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 