val containing points on both sides is not one-to-one: inputs equally far from the vertex have the same output.\n\n- Interval $x\\in [-1,0)$, $[-1,0)$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $0\\le \\frac{1}{2}$. It is therefore invertible.\n\n- Interval $x\\in [\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$, $[\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $\\frac{1}{2}\\ge \\frac{1}{2}$. It is therefore invertible.\n\n- Interval $x\\in (0,1]$, $(0,1]$, contains the distinct inputs $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\frac{3}{4}$, both with output $\\frac{1}{16}$. It is therefore not invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-1,0)$; $x\\in [\\frac{1}{2},\\frac{3}{2})$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513226 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124474 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "149fa184-850f-52d8-a309-4b79a371a74d" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intervals on Which a Function is Invertible Given a Description"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e2f0ce7-9862-5266-b3e7-f2842be0d59d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513206} {:answer/id #uuid "752a6a84-a836-5529-8e6b-bf3083cc174f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e2f0ce7-9862-5266-b3e7-f2842be0d59d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513206} :answer-field/id #uuid "11109a7d-017c-5747-aa35-8cfeec4328e3" :answer-field/key "$x\\in [-1,0)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513183} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2ab3fb1d-8c0a-5674-ab13-610877e1e042" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 1759218651319