tion is strictly monotone. Including the vertex as an endpoint does not create a repeated output. An interval containing points on both sides is not one-to-one: inputs equally far from the vertex have the same output.\n\n- Interval $x\\in [-1,0)$, $[-1,0)$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $0\\le \\frac{1}{2}$. It is therefore invertible.\n\n- Interval $x\\in (1,2]$, $(1,2]$, lies on one side of the vertex, since $1\\ge \\frac{1}{2}$. It is therefore invertible.\n\n- Interval $x\\in (0,1]$, $(0,1]$, contains the distinct inputs $\\frac{1}{4}$ and $\\frac{3}{4}$, both with output $\\frac{1}{16}$. It is therefore not invertible.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $x\\in [-1,0)$; $x\\in (1,2]$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513492 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068695 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1d6997e4-f1cf-5e31-ac04-69d7b108bf4c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513494} {:answer/id #uuid "aa8f16f0-8d91-524d-a6aa-056212c928df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513506}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa8f16f0-8d91-524d-a6aa-056212c928df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513506} :answer-field/id #uuid "7b336a22-ce20-5a6b-8abb-1b2bf6621e0a" :answer-field/key "$x=- \\frac{1}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513501} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1966c371-f5cd-533a-b50b-c25d3af12bab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/re