=- \\frac{3}{2}.$ Since there is a jump at $x=- \\frac{3}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{3}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=- \\frac{1}{2}.$ Since there is a break at $x=- \\frac{1}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{1}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is  $x=\\frac{1}{2}$ only.\n\n \n\n![](images/4d/4db3d16c1d05cf201e94dcbb7a8e53f82e412aa9d70a72c9766022b5d2d79466.png)"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186513495 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068695 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "6cd6c125-ecaf-5847-a802-ec1b3594a15c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether a Function Is Continuous at a Given Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4da50c13-2696-580a-aedc-1db9b42c0734" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513498} {:answer/id #uuid "5726127b-42eb-5208-9bc6-de3b5a702723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513499}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5726127b-42eb-5208-9bc6-de3b5a702723" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513499} :answer-field/id #uuid "35c3db6c-165a-54e7-83a5-f0703881c30f" :answer-field/key "$x=- \\frac{3}{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186513496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b4f6c0ea-5692-5763-9248-dc51a93c1d5a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/v