continuous at $x=- \\frac{9}{2}.$ Because there is a jump at $x=- \\frac{9}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{9}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is continuous at $x=-3.$ The graph can be drawn in the neighborhood of $x=-3$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\n- The function $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=- \\frac{3}{2}.$ Since there is a break at $x=- \\frac{3}{2},$ it is impossible to draw the function in the neighborhood of $x=- \\frac{3}{2}$ without taking our pencil off of the paper.\n\nHence, the correct answer is: $x=-3$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3f74909d-3917-5c2c-ab2f-dd1b795a3b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515929} {:answer/id #uuid "e4e63d41-590c-51d9-be3e-9529b97aa13f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3f74909d-3917-5c2c-ab2f-dd1b795a3b27" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515929} :answer-field/id #uuid "58d19d64-0412-5d33-bb62-bc6da3b833f8" :answer-field/key "The zeros of the function are exactly $x=n\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515937} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3f6b5ee-38f3-5b40-85a8-9992cbe5a3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515969} {:answer/id #uuid "a78b662a-1866-5d3a-9082-787353e6d592" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515970}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a3f6b5ee-38f3-5b40-85a8-9992cbe5a3e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515969} :answer-field/id #uuid "697f706a-db33-5589-87cb-f6bb5a07193d" :answer-field/key "The vertical asymptotes are exactly $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515944} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "798ef0e1-48c8-530a-81db-9a4a0aa42ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515951} {:answer/id #uuid "feba7162-d932-5146-90aa-e0386fd42d87" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516014}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "798ef0e1-48c8-530a-81db-9a4a0aa42ac1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515951} :answer-field/id #uuid "fb3f4145-d21c-57db-a5fa-197de63efd53" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $[-1,1].$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516009}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0611bd23-ee0e-588d-8010-4f01ff7ae188" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The zeros of the function are exactly $x=n\\pi.$” is true. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm\\pi,\\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The vertical asymptotes are exactly $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$” is true. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The range of the function is $[-1,1].$” is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The zeros of the function are exactly $x=n\\pi.$”; “The vertical asymptotes are exactly $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "75a178e2-b8a0-5e23-95d8-57e0b22e66e8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515948} {:answer/id #uuid "cea54101-9dc1-513c-8325-1c76ddfeb073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515989}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cea54101-9dc1-513c-8325-1c76ddfeb073" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515989} :answer-field/id #uuid "131a63aa-afd8-5dd6-98ab-74699ace8718" :answer-field/key "The domain is all real numbers." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515920} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f0a2436-d2b8-5ada-bc74-03b482439509" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515917} {:answer/id #uuid "2d3d707f-8861-51cf-bd71-44eb3c3678ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d3d707f-8861-51cf-bd71-44eb3c3678ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515924} :answer-field/id #uuid "8b59ef31-8c85-53fa-af26-f5a8104dc0e2" :answer-field/key "The least positive period is $\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515960} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37f2a0ca-c13a-53b6-8fde-b6f03e923b0e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515927} {:answer/id #uuid "93abb7ed-08f3-5fe3-b5e8-61618de9def4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515961}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "93abb7ed-08f3-5fe3-b5e8-61618de9def4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515961} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5c77fec-21b9-5241-91cb-3a7932d621ee" :answer-field/key "The function is negative throughout $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi,n\\pi).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516000}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "34e68721-06df-5e4c-ae2f-a9024e61fe8c" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The domain is all real numbers” is false. The function is defined everywhere except where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The function is negative throughout $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi,n\\pi).$” is true. The function is positive on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and negative on $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0).$ The period is $\\pi,$ so these signs repeat after each integer multiple of $\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The least positive period is $\\pi.$” is true. The graph repeats after a horizontal shift of $\\pi,$ and no smaller positive shift repeats the whole graph. Therefore, the least positive period is $\\pi.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The function is negative throughout $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi,n\\pi).$”; “The least positive period is $\\pi.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515938 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0216de2e-4a0f-57e3-9b57-0ff0f473bd35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515915} {:answer/id #uuid "cb9acb2e-307a-5bff-84df-1d99817452ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cb9acb2e-307a-5bff-84df-1d99817452ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515986} :answer-field/id #uuid "11def7b4-86ae-5083-b3a6-95ac3f063630" :answer-field/key "The range of the function is $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},\\frac{\\pi}{2}).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515919} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "579b7bf4-e674-5a6e-b50f-733059831e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.