tatement.\n\n- Statement “The zeros of the function are exactly $x=n\\pi.$” is true. The zeros occur at $x=0,\\pm\\pi,\\pm2\\pi,\\ldots,$ which can be written as $x=n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The vertical asymptotes are exactly $x=2n\\pi.$” is false. The function has an asymptote at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}$ and the period is $\\pi.$ Therefore, the asymptotes occur at $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The range of the function is $(0,\\infty).$” is false. The function takes values on all the real numbers, hence the range is $(-\\infty,\\infty).$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The zeros of the function are exactly $x=n\\pi.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515965 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9606e487-0713-51cd-8d7b-86344299b977" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515964} {:answer/id #uuid "bd35cfd0-28c3-566f-b8e3-4d292de9e5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "bd35cfd0-28c3-566f-b8e3-4d292de9e5fc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515979} :answer-field/id #uuid "442f3a19-905b-523f-b1f9-f30240a29310" :answer-field/key "The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515930} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c26246b2-ee13-51b7-9e93-524ec615af29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515982} {:answer/id #uuid "f0f03165-7735-5013-924c-72f36254f7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516003}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f0f03165-7735-5013-924c-72f36254f7c7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516003} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a03890b-f8e9-5a96-8bd7-d6ef8a3efdee" :answer-field/key "The function has no positive period." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515952} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "76f3739f-3d95-5f10-9e90-1ba5246e8957" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515949} {:answer/id #uuid "a792c3b8-b6dd-5cfb-9674-2e56d346de23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a792c3b8-b6dd-5cfb-9674-2e56d346de23" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515971} :answer-field/id #uuid "b695a7a6-9766-58f8-a0a0-616c0947a9ef" :answer-field/key "The function is negative throughout $(n\\pi,\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi).$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515977}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9792d956-ea77-5200-b68a-06624704ecdd" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$” is true. The function is defined everywhere except where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The function is negative throughout $(n\\pi,\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi).$” is false. The function is positive on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and negative on $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0).$ The period is $\\pi,$ so these signs repeat after each integer multiple of $\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The function has no positive period” is false. The graph repeats after a horizontal shift of $\\pi,$ and no smaller positive shift repeats the whole graph. Therefore, the least positive period is $\\pi.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515981 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176049 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4241c7bd-4a2b-556f-be9f-8a884addebb9" :knowledge-point/title "Describing Properties of the Tangent Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59e0e97e-5cea-5f1e-8e24-1bc56a216407" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515939} {:answer/id #uuid "cdb4548a-d120-590b-a1a0-91a4dd318d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515988}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cdb4548a-d120-590b-a1a0-91a4dd318d6f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515988} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f45d56-bc6a-56f7-8662-5c8c4c1866d2" :answer-field/key "The least positive period is $\\pi.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515921} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3099072b-d865-56fd-a07b-65485f9ab3fe" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/valu