ing the function $y=\\tan x?$ Assume that $n$ is an integer.\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\tan x.$\n\n![](images/e6/e65a2728d8bdad40af736ced1ec8303bf10fb4d11fc66b33784663512093a26b.png)\n\nLet's go through each statement.\n\n- Statement “The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$” is true. The function is defined everywhere except where $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The function is positive throughout $(n\\pi,\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi).$” is true. The function is positive on $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$ and negative on $(-\\frac{\\pi}{2},0).$ The period is $\\pi,$ so these signs repeat after each integer multiple of $\\pi.$\n\n- Statement “The least positive period is $2\\pi.$” is false. The graph repeats after a horizontal shift of $\\pi,$ and no smaller positive shift repeats the whole graph. Therefore, the least positive period is $\\pi.$\n\nSo, the correct answer is “The domain is all real numbers except $x=\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi.$”; “The function is positive throughout $(n\\pi,\\frac{\\pi}{2}+n\\pi).$” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517000 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e6bab16-c48f-5d71-ba04-cf367cce07b6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516997} {:answer/id #uuid "667b9553-a43f-59bc-b1b6-5bed93f5c4ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517035}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "667b9553-a43f-59bc-b1b6-5bed93f5c4ad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517035} :answer-field/id #uuid "