ion $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The range of the function is $(-\\infty,-1]\\cup[1,\\infty)$.  Hence, statement “The range is all real numbers” is false.\n\n- The graph does not intersect the $y$-axis, as $x=0$ is not in the domain. Hence, statement “The graph does not intersect the $y$-axis” is true.\n\n- The range is unbounded above and below, so the function has no global minimum or maximum. Hence, statement “The function has no global minimum or maximum” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "454820d6-a5f0-56e6-b8e6-96274b650934" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517019} {:answer/id #uuid "e4c1d33e-9364-594c-8519-61a5af0b4f3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517085}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "454820d6-a5f0-56e6-b8e6-96274b650934" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517019} :answer-field/id #uuid "75520965-5e52-58bd-9fdd-b7cc3e312072" :answer-field/key "The point $(\\frac{9\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517042} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "435434a0-59e2-5c23-843b-8dc1a9d71c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517017} {:answer/id #uuid "51410d88-b1a6-5ba9-87b6-29af36c17940" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517027}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "435434a0-59e2-5c23-843b-8dc1a9d71c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517017} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dad2840-782d-5d64-92c4-5ba4946194c4" :answer-field/key "$x=11\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517053} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "620189dd-e716-5a6f-941c-41f3b1f6bed5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517033} {:answer/id #uuid "cab7e494-6c3d-53de-bdc0-7127833308ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cab7e494-6c3d-53de-bdc0-7127833308ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517072} :answer-field/id #uuid "922ddb9a-fd35-5f64-a9ac-56848dbbabfa" :answer-field/key "$x=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517055}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f88d4101-5b98-5a6e-abf9-19b6874206de" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement “The point $(\\frac{9\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph” is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement “$x=11\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote” is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is not an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement “$x=\\frac{7\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186517095 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186176053 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92d6129b-a5c5-597a-86ee-3f19af20f326" :knowledge-point/title "Describing the General Properties of the Cosecant Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e08accb-7eda-5b3f-8f7f-cf6049c19834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517023} {:answer/id #uuid "53ceef81-cbcf-5469-a654-9c8dc64c15b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517029}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e08accb-7eda-5b3f-8f7f-cf6049c19834" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517023} :answer-field/id #uuid "01a3e318-485f-572e-9d51-28ff9e7bc115" :answer-field/key "The point $(\\frac{9\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516987} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d9fcad0-b7c1-5b69-9f63-65e152eb6676" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517011} {:answer/id #uuid "ba6d4175-e2fb-5a81-aa89-ea597fed72d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517067}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba6d4175-e2fb-5a81-aa89-ea597fed72d0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517067} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b450d50-fe98-5b6a-bbb9-5b94a6399b59" :answer-field/key "$x=\\frac{-4\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517004} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "879bbe6d-6321-5aa6-9fca-0e98609ffa91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517051} {:answer/id #uuid "8837bdf2-18a9-5865-b0d8-61465361cb77" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517052}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "879bbe6d-6321-5aa6-9fca-0e98609ffa91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517051} :answer-field/id #uuid "628f5a29-72f4-5abf-8e2c-51bccdc1b9fa" :answer-field/key "$x=-3\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186517034}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "fb8b6ba6-3782-5361-89b1-1ab426047925" :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function $y=\\csc x$?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's plot the graph of $y=\\csc x.$\n\n![](images/f1/f1b80c29b8f9f4d33aae94fc287d95b97cc5865b36ecc98f4f41e625dfc842e1.png)\n\nNow, let's go through each statement.\n\n- The cosecant takes the value $1$ at $x=\\frac{9\\pi }{2}$. Hence, statement “The point $(\\frac{9\\pi }{2},-1)$ is on the graph” is false.\n\n- The lines $x=n\\pi$ for any integer $n$ are the vertical asymptotes of the function. Hence, statement “$x=-3\\pi $ is a vertical asymptote” is true.\n\n- The domain excludes exactly the integer multiples of $\\pi$. The number $\\frac{-4\\pi }{2}$ is an integer multiple of $\\pi$. Hence, statement “$x=\\frac{-4\\pi }{2}$ is in the domain” is false."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518349 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9989dcac-70d7-5630-bdf4-c565b6f5338a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518391} {:answer/id #uuid "adb1be5c-c6af-5de1-a9de-5ef1f6ffdc82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518395}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9989dcac-70d7-5630-bdf4-c565b6f5338a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518391} :answer-field/id #uuid "17e3bfdb-da57-5a10-b6e3-4c54386afa1a" :answer-field/key "$p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518356} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "04495513-6bec-5b14-9226-a23b006ae8cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518347} {:answer/id #uuid "d792b3a0-5abf-5621-9e5d-957ac21b3b8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518408}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "04495513-6bec-5b14-9226-a23b006ae8cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518347} :answer-field/id #uuid "2d03423c-ba74-55fa-86ea-c7195a1f73c1" :answer-field/key "$p(0)$ is positive." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518361} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c26ac2a-dba6-5ec4-80f8-13843d41e251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518383} {:answer/id #uuid "db0d94bb-b1f6-5e17-9118-b2086a5b4080" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518410}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c26ac2a-dba6-5ec4-80f8-13843d41e251" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518383} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d537d62-6492-5747-b026-17962779dd51" :answer-field/key "$x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0a9a6af0-71e4-5dc9-94f7-baab6024584a" :question/problem "![](images/e3/e394351bcb1baa70d140355d41b1266789866fbc683018fcc9a252a220b54f12.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$p(0)$ is positive” is false. The graph passes through the $y$-axis at $y=0,$ which means that $p(0)=0.$\n\n- Statement “$p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$” is true. As $x$ moves right in the positive direction towards $\\infty ,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative direction towards $-\\infty .$\n\n- Statement “$x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity” is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$p(x)\\to -\\infty $ as $x\\to \\infty .$”; “$x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity” only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14cf9c72-4cdb-5aa6-a64e-41c5c19c3b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518354} {:answer/id #uuid "1b91876e-3aca-572d-bee9-86c13299e1b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518357}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14cf9c72-4cdb-5aa6-a64e-41c5c19c3b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518354} :answer-field/id #uuid "0fb96147-e282-57f4-a2f5-92e488fccefb" :answer-field/key "$x=-1$ is a simple root." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518352} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "736f6911-2e4f-57fb-a60e-65e3bf78faf1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518375} {:answer/id #uuid "c36f2e01-c37d-502c-91d5-48acdcee0823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518398}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c36f2e01-c37d-502c-91d5-48acdcee0823" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518398} :answer-field/id #uuid "1bd23ced-a696-583a-9d49-327608baf82f" :answer-field/key "$x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518358} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92bbf3e6-a040-53be-9087-8ff5d1ed39c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518387} {:answer/id #uuid "e870fec8-e19b-50cb-80b9-e545176f2a31" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518411}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92bbf3e6-a040-53be-9087-8ff5d1ed39c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518387} :answer-field/id #uuid "4058cb5a-0762-5580-a235-6fa4c2ed6b0c" :answer-field/key "$x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518365}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f58ad4d-7f2e-5f82-a45b-d443ba532270" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f88a8daa307b97157b5088ef25c469d7534cfc89f707dcd25eb880a406df4ae9.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$x=-1$ is a simple root” is true. The root $x=-1$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the \n$x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point.\n\n- Statement “$x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity” is true. The root $x=0$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point.\n\n- Statement “$x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity” is true. The root $x=1$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=1$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is “$x=-1$ is a simple root”; “$x=0$ is a root of odd multiplicity”; “$x=1$ is a root of even multiplicity”."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186518368 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129154 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a66188f6-3228-59e9-9766-0f9bacbe8443" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying True Statements Regarding the Graph of a Given Polynomial"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31eea996-df1c-5e9a-b396-762556217d49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518362} {:answer/id #uuid "c7ce711f-719f-5eb2-8b6a-a2cd987e792f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518400}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c7ce711f-719f-5eb2-8b6a-a2cd987e792f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518400} :answer-field/id #uuid "8dcb5725-6f3b-59da-a545-58f3c66a476e" :answer-field/key "$x=-4$ is a root of even multiplicity." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518385} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b3d7777-55d8-5df3-a9e8-bc3d671d57a6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518350} {:answer/id #uuid "14a18e20-4955-5276-8c78-23057fd0b2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518353}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "14a18e20-4955-5276-8c78-23057fd0b2da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518353} :answer-field/id #uuid "9558d40d-6580-5054-a1eb-9a287079f2ba" :answer-field/key "$p(x)\\to -\\infty$ as $x\\to -\\infty.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518388} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d307fb3-0518-5fac-b624-e01c94fd256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518392} {:answer/id #uuid "cac0a315-b600-575b-978d-f641b8c46dff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518402}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d307fb3-0518-5fac-b624-e01c94fd256b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518392} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e5483a5-c655-56be-b5fe-7770a9454395" :answer-field/key "$x=-5$ and $x=3$ are simple roots." :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186518393}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "456c228f-2e6f-567b-929e-ea2ba65e9871" :question/problem "![](images/2f/2f5db590b02f2aa9ec604f7fa5ebbf0afc5bcb2cd3505b49e092715bc55dc346.png)\n\nThe graph of a polynomial $p(x)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement “$x=-5$ and $x=3$ are simple roots” is false. The root $x=-5$ is a simple root because the graph crosses the $x$-axis at the point and the curve is not tangent to the $x$-axis at that point. The root $x=3$ has an odd multiplicity because the graph passes through the $x$-axis at this point. The curve is tangent to the $x$-axis at that point, so the root is not simple.\n\n- Statement “$x=-4$ is a root of even multiplicity” is true. The root $x=-4$ has an even multiplicity because at $x=-4$ the graph just touches the $x$-axis and reverses direction.\n\n- Statement “$p(x)\\to -\\infty$ as $x\\to -\\infty.$” is true. As $x$ moves left in the negative direction towards $-\\infty,$ the $y$ value moves down in the negative 