begin{aligned}8 x y + 3 y^{2}&=16 x^{2} + 1024\\\\- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 16 x^{2} + 8 x y + 3 y^{2} - 1024)\\,j\\\\&=(8 x + 6 y)\\,i-(- 32 x + 8 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\32 x - 8 y&=0\\\\y&=4x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=4x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}3(4x)^{2}+8x(4x)-16x^{2}-1024&=0\\\\64x^{2}-1024&=0\\\\x^{2}&=16\\\\x&=\\pm 4\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(4,16)$ and $(-4,-16)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521807 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a081b4b-d2c2-54f6-ab72-e97e24330f29" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521827} {:answer/id #uuid "f122121f-13ed-5d40-84a7-05ee73afda8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f122121f-13ed-5d40-84a7-05ee73afda8c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521871} :answer-field/id #uuid "31f0b4d9-85ff-5f7b-a017-2aaa76c4d97a" :answer-field/key "$(\\frac{1}{2},4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #e