" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521772} {:answer/id #uuid "2a4d2807-65a8-535d-b28f-d716f496cbc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2a4d2807-65a8-535d-b28f-d716f496cbc5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521773} :answer-field/id #uuid "f01ae0ea-77c1-50d9-838c-8c96b77ae81a" :answer-field/key "$(-2,-4)$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f0a0a0dc-dc0e-505f-ae57-9fc7b81e15fb" :question/problem "At which points on the curve $4 x y + 2 y^{2}=4 x^{2} + 48$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $j$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}4 x y + 2 y^{2}&=4 x^{2} + 48\\\\- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48&=0\\end{aligned}$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=0.$\n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$t(x,y)=f_y(x,y)\\,i-f_x(x,y)\\,j$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)&=\\frac{∂}{∂y}(- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48)\\,i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(- 4 x^{2} + 4 x y + 2 y^{2} - 48)\\,j\\\\&=(4 x + 4 y)\\,i-(- 8 x + 4 y)\\,j\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $j$, we must have $t\\cdot j=0.$\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot j&=0\\\\8 x - 4 y&=0\\\\y&=2x\\end{aligned}$$\n\nSubstituting $y=2x$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\\begin{aligned}2(2x)^{2}+4x(2x)-4x^{2}-48&=0\\\\12x^{2}-48&=0\\\\x^{2}&=4\\\\x&=\\pm 2\\end{aligned}$$\n\nFinally, the corresponding points are $(2,4)$ and $(-2,-4)$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521880 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "27cae781-a5b1-5d1a-a336-28677997d8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521883} {:answer/id #uuid "43adf706-556a-5541-95dd-e56f093e98a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521892}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "27cae781-a5b1-5d1a-a336-28677997d8d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521883} :answer-field/id #uuid "300668c7-94d5-5a1d-96ad-33fc31a43286" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521885} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3e4dc9fc-e868-51af-82a5-75a6f76b6034" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521891} {:answer/id #uuid "5ba55c1e-3fc6-5f75-8886-bffde1bc1542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521898}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5ba55c1e-3fc6-5f75-8886-bffde1bc1542" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521898} :answer-field/id #uuid "3578c6fd-9b36-5337-acfe-ed0b376c2c06" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521888} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "833b8aa4-8f0f-54f8-bcd0-ad0222a4dce7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521902} {:answer/id #uuid "afffdfaf-7ad9-5a48-8093-c75db5af7af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "afffdfaf-7ad9-5a48-8093-c75db5af7af8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521911} :answer-field/id #uuid "74c7a9f5-1b9e-5e24-8415-8f6301839038" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{5}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521901}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1180df6e-fa40-51b3-98ac-1d4f6fae04df" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{25{t}^{2}+7},\\,5t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{3}{5} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+7},\\,2u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$ is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{2k}{5}$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+7},\\,0\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521893 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09ea6799-2d9f-5f37-95ae-72f2a5e9ca76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521879} {:answer/id #uuid "396d5a0c-09ce-5ae5-a8e9-bb9f1699e6cc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "09ea6799-2d9f-5f37-95ae-72f2a5e9ca76" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521879} :answer-field/id #uuid "035d8c2d-9be7-5bbc-921f-3a6f151dc7d1" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=5k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521878} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a2370a66-c29c-5b37-89c6-2da05967bf6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521907} {:answer/id #uuid "d4d2de1b-0311-5bc7-9aee-5e7fbdce2a1d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521915}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a2370a66-c29c-5b37-89c6-2da05967bf6a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521907} :answer-field/id #uuid "34f3798f-9a31-575e-a080-fbc367dd1750" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521886} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3f12a61-204a-52df-a045-31308fbcfe09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521914} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5f2c45-a77f-5e71-a3fb-27da4adb38d5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521920}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3f12a61-204a-52df-a045-31308fbcfe09" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521914} :answer-field/id #uuid "367a4648-c48b-5ca7-beb6-0362f0f20418" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521889}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "44945cc2-d075-5615-b775-29cceef305cf" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨4t,\\,6\\sqrt{t}⟩, & 0\\le t\\le 5 \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨20u,\\,6\\sqrt{5u}⟩, & 0\\le u\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ is true, while statement ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=5k$ is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\ny=\\sqrt{9x},\\,0\\le x\\le 20.\n$$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$; ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "54b68761-81ae-5727-8723-99155f456d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521896} {:answer/id #uuid "c0e75279-2f6c-585f-a49b-30410cd91345" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521912}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "54b68761-81ae-5727-8723-99155f456d21" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521896} :answer-field/id #uuid "353ba0ff-733c-57e5-8e81-74317481335b" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{5k}{4}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521887} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03178fdc-25eb-592a-aa45-4e266963dfb8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521877} {:answer/id #uuid "f9cde8a0-0128-565a-a4cd-433dec39fb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f9cde8a0-0128-565a-a4cd-433dec39fb80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521925} :answer-field/id #uuid "84208a78-46f7-5cc8-aae2-ed3bf108cc3d" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521903} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6080977b-5766-59b3-82b0-9891037d1857" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521899} {:answer/id #uuid "f5c7ad3d-6caa-593c-b2d1-652348ed0ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521922}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f5c7ad3d-6caa-593c-b2d1-652348ed0ede" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521922} :answer-field/id #uuid "a38cc838-6019-5577-98f0-f639569b05e7" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521908}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8b2a59b4-567e-519b-bf4b-185eb8ce7675" :question/problem "Consider the curves ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2},$ defined parametrically as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{C}_{1}:\\,{r}_{1}(t) & =⟨\\sqrt{16{t}^{2}+6},\\,4t⟩, & 0\\le t\\le \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ {C}_{2}:\\,{r}_{2}(u) & =⟨\\sqrt{25{u}^{2}+6},\\,5u⟩, & 0\\le u\\le \\frac{2}{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ for some function $f(x,y)$ and real number $k.$ Which of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-k$ is false. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=\\frac{5k}{4}$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ is true. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{{y}^{2}+6},\\,0\\le y\\le 2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=k$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521916 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12383e44-707a-5bdc-aed6-bacd5d241604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521881} {:answer/id #uuid "d39317c7-f550-51db-95fa-14ecef4d8119" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521913}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "12383e44-707a-5bdc-aed6-bacd5d241604" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521881} :answer-field/id #uuid "2849e85a-9324-5c9e-8606-379763c5280c" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨243{u}^{4}-18{u}^{2},\\,3u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521884} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66fdd48e-d5d5-5dab-826a-ac4be0dd2146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521900} {:answer/id #uuid "f63ced98-a9ce-5a73-aa16-45250abe7b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f63ced98-a9ce-5a73-aa16-45250abe7b46" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521923} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b47340d-4902-5241-a3d9-513d7bd87af2" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521895} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f2c947ff-8de3-54d5-9100-bb93fe81f325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521921} {:answer/id #uuid "f7971d96-ca08-549f-84cc-5b72709d09cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521924}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f7971d96-ca08-549f-84cc-5b72709d09cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521924} :answer-field/id #uuid "dcd179a6-c2d5-5420-98bf-79fb4b48750e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d7163cdf-b4ca-5487-945d-916df17c97fc" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-2{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 3.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-1$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=3,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨243{u}^{4}-18{u}^{2},\\,3u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$” is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=3{y}^{4}-2{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=1$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186521917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162083 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "96d48adf-a293-54ae-88fd-ee8471e5fc65" :knowledge-point/title "Applying Independence of Parametrization and Orientation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5a9f9a52-3082-5433-95a4-c5f4c8ae8cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521897} {:answer/id #uuid "e91b5391-28fc-5690-8b2d-39d3a871a375" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5a9f9a52-3082-5433-95a4-c5f4c8ae8cd8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521897} :answer-field/id #uuid "1993f2eb-5838-569b-889b-81d0a604df5e" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521882} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3df0d4d-09b8-5201-b83b-666c7581491b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521909} {:answer/id #uuid "fbf41162-0ae6-5fde-a058-b41d64e5185f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521926}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fbf41162-0ae6-5fde-a058-b41d64e5185f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521926} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fd61f71-05fe-55f1-b853-74a722e4ca24" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=16,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨768{u}^{4}-64{u}^{2},\\,4u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521906} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4b1d7ba5-ad3e-5ada-b964-6c10ca778eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521894} {:answer/id #uuid "847b701e-4db4-558f-93db-2cb8924742bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "847b701e-4db4-558f-93db-2cb8924742bb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521904} :answer-field/id #uuid "a7dc35ec-2dc1-528e-a10f-cea74dd734d7" :answer-field/key "${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186521910}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "dc964df5-3846-54bf-91a3-d8d19abd4103" :question/problem "Suppose ${\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$ for some function $f(x,y),$ where ${C}_{1}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{1}(t)=⟨3{t}^{4}-4{t}^{2},\\,t⟩$ for $0\\le t\\le 4.$\n\nWhich of the following must be true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parametrization and orientation.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each statement. \n\n- Statement ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=-4$ is false, while statement ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$ is true. Reversing the curve's orientation does *not* change the value of a line integral with respect to arc length. Therefore, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s={\\int }_{{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n- Statement “${\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=16,$ where ${C}_{2}$ is parametrized by ${r}_{2}(u)=⟨768{u}^{4}-64{u}^{2},\\,4u⟩$ for $0\\le u\\le 1.$” is false. Notice that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ are different parameterizations of the same curve. Since line integrals with respect to arc length are independent of the choice of parameterization, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{{C}_{2}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4.\n$$\n\n \nTo see that ${C}_{1}$ and ${C}_{2}$ represent the same curve, we can convert each parametrization to Cartesian form. In doing so, we find that both parameterizations give the Cartesian curve\n\n$$\nx=3{y}^{4}-4{y}^{2},\\,0\\le y\\le 4.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is ${\\int }_{-{C}_{1}}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}s=4$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523101 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "46fe9d86-8a7b-5b31-9f33-352086d9b0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523118} {:answer/id #uuid "58a2e68c-7ee5-5893-a320-e4d59782d97a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523127}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "46fe9d86-8a7b-5b31-9f33-352086d9b0be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523118} :answer-field/id #uuid "072bdae2-59da-58c7-af80-28f3f2f9aae7" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523094} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02336600-7104-5fb9-9b31-cae1a52518dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523092} {:answer/id #uuid "547d116e-af59-5ba8-b479-146d79b8a167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523124}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "547d116e-af59-5ba8-b479-146d79b8a167" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523124} :answer-field/id #uuid "2c4297dc-f995-5396-8e9e-d024c65ce177" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523113} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "141e0203-23b8-5619-a962-5626778a971c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523103} {:answer/id #uuid "6fb4a988-bcd2-5b80-a37e-65bc083843a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523137}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "141e0203-23b8-5619-a962-5626778a971c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523103} :answer-field/id #uuid "60631e67-ec0e-5269-b67b-3fd99562c886" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523131}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1080e551-06cd-5714-8bdc-170d1f4b1992" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y &=0 \\\\ x+4y &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 4\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere is a pivot for each variable and no contradictory row. The system has a unique solution, so we conclude that the system is consistent independent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent independent” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523112 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e065480-c3c7-5a97-80dd-f851baccc4cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523108} {:answer/id #uuid "63fa15da-a612-551e-bc84-28195f146d91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523135}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63fa15da-a612-551e-bc84-28195f146d91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523135} :answer-field/id #uuid "95720269-0a64-5442-8ea6-fada3caa3f3d" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523154} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a075d6f9-6a6b-521c-9a45-cefd6406a87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523157} {:answer/id #uuid "a3d89df8-a864-501a-978f-d1b4c908a594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523159}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a075d6f9-6a6b-521c-9a45-cefd6406a87f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523157} :answer-field/id #uuid "d4f4634b-41cc-5f87-b51b-46f0fed4e546" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523175} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c51d359e-c96e-568d-a08a-cc6a5975c003" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523169} {:answer/id #uuid "d80969b7-edb9-54aa-9415-47b2ca6fa4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d80969b7-edb9-54aa-9415-47b2ca6fa4d6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523176} :answer-field/id #uuid "da426b62-5fc6-56a5-92f1-825ae424ef78" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523179}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "2c37a8ce-9961-58b3-83eb-74946c8f3663" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y-2z &=-4 \\\\ x+3y &=-8 \\\\ x+y-4z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 3 & 0 & -8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & -4 & -3\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(1){R}_{2} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe final row corresponds to the equation $0x+0y+0z=-3,$ and this has no solution. Therefore, our system has no solution, and we conclude that the system is inconsistent.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is inconsistent” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523119 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92f5b3ce-9f77-555e-a32f-418bc4e4ae3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523151} {:answer/id #uuid "9552d211-6758-511e-9dd2-695af0b42a16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523153}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "92f5b3ce-9f77-555e-a32f-418bc4e4ae3e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523151} :answer-field/id #uuid "178e2ad7-57e9-5728-a5d6-b6e9f1ddc32e" :answer-field/key "The system is inconsistent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1127203c-eb67-5f24-9963-9f6c74e2e286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523102} {:answer/id #uuid "7b3c86e8-fe67-5803-979e-32951465e4ec" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523140}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1127203c-eb67-5f24-9963-9f6c74e2e286" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523102} :answer-field/id #uuid "8925e95f-c16a-5da9-bc62-4ffcfe2c9609" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent dependent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6f9e16b-ee78-5f24-a114-9509d560608d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523162} {:answer/id #uuid "ffb07647-4604-59aa-a0cf-ee179bfdcceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523191}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ffb07647-4604-59aa-a0cf-ee179bfdcceb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523191} :answer-field/id #uuid "d98057d3-cab1-5021-9e07-c30835639d6d" :answer-field/key "The system is consistent independent" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523177}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "482e6d01-f9bf-525e-86f9-c527dca5de7f" :question/problem "Consider the following system of equations.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-3y &=-5 \\\\ -2x+6y &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "To classify the system, we first need to find its solution. The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nUsing the method of Gaussian elimination, we can reduce this matrix to row echelon form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & 10\\end{bmatrix} & {R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(2){R}_{1} \\\\ & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. Here there is one free variable, $y$. Therefore, since there are infinitely many solutions, we conclude that the system is *consistent dependent*.\n\nAs a result, only statement “The system is consistent dependent” is true."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523120 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115299 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f9469d5c-e097-590c-8ddb-2c7fda353fac" :knowledge-point/title "Classifying a System as Consistent Dependent, Consistent Independent, or Inconsistent"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4094b2ed-2795-574f-9bb3-fb2c83ecb51c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523117} {:answer/id #uuid "5f0b8de0-9754-5abb-bbaa-1a2488a781e3" :answer/ty