46139} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e36f489-1c4c-526c-94f3-98e4e077cd62" :answer-field/key "$A(t)=\\langle 2t, t^2, 1\\rangle$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186546191}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "c4594d22-501e-5549-8493-0b63014fe436" :question/problem "Which of the following are vector fields on $\\mathbb R^3?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of $\\mathbb R^3.$ A vector field on $\\mathbb R^3$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $A(t)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $B(t)$ is *not* a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns points in $\\mathbb R$ (not $\\mathbb R^3$) to vectors in $\\mathbb R^3$.\n\n- The function $C(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on $\\mathbb R^3.$ It assigns every point $(x,y,z)\\in\\mathbb R^3$ to a vector in $\\mathbb R^3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $C(x,y,z)=\\langle 2x, x^2, 1\\rangle$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557709 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "bf82865b-b7f8-5978-a65d-6ceaeecc7985" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557768} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c67902-8586-522d-8128-26d6372edb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d2c67902-8586-522d-8128-26d6372edb3c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557777} :answer-field/id #uuid "352475c6-893f-5d15-8bd4-4fc7d65c9b40" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557713} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e8f869e2-c759-591a-9c02-906bc98f760f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557789} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e346c7-807b-58b0-9826-de71aa5abe49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557791}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e9e346c7-807b-58b0-9826-de71aa5abe49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557791} :answer-field/id #uuid "5aac40eb-e4b1-5a40-92f2-d09ca0cd77c3" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557725} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "023a940e-0586-53bb-85a2-7d425b0cf6a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557703} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4cf946-1ca5-5f24-9b50-8c5503ce3a04" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557758}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "023a940e-0586-53bb-85a2-7d425b0cf6a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557703} :answer-field/id #uuid "765fa93c-fc92-5c91-8fc2-7219896e12df" :answer-field/key "$B={A}^{-1}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557736}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1a0b8b2e-0993-564b-9de2-b414008b167b" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $AB=BA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AB$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ ∗ & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AB=BA={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $B\\ne {A}^{-1}$ and statement $B={A}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\n- Now, we check whether $AC=CA={I}_{2}.$ Computing $AC$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $CA$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CA & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{4} & -\\frac{3}{4} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -\\frac{3}{2} \\\\ -1 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $AC=CA={I}_{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557710 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-poi