$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557784}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "933e41fa-bbab-5d05-965d-5162035714bc" :question/problem "Consider the matrices\n\n$$\nE=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,F=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,G=\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- First, we check whether $EF=FE={I}_{2}.$ Computing $EF$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EF & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLikewise, computing $FE$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}FE & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{3}{4} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{2}.\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $EF=FE={I}_{2}$ is true.\n\n- Now, we check whether $EG=GE={I}_{2}.$ Computing $EG$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}EG & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4} & -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}∗ & ∗ \\\\ \\frac{3}{2} & ∗\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & \\ne {I}_{2}.\\,\\times \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, statement $EG=GE={I}_{2}$ is false. As a result, $G\\ne {E}^{-1}$ and statement $G={E}^{-1}$ is false too.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is $EF=FE={I}_{2}$ only."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186557746 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087699 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9b9ef325-2358-5041-8a8d-b459e8ed9f09" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35a0f523-b1e4-57b4-8986-3d408f116ada" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557715} {:answer/id #uuid "4f30ad3a-ebca-54d0-80d8-eb5e24d49530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557720}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4f30ad3a-ebca-54d0-80d8-eb5e24d49530" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557720} :answer-field/id #uuid "8f860d9c-0f4b-51cc-941b-fa8e0bb36f8f" :answer-field/key "$AC=CA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557743} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "539f2745-380c-5c87-9c4b-698d2d8a5ae1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557722} {:answer/id #uuid "e59853dc-024a-5613-8bda-a7a5ad6a4077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e59853dc-024a-5613-8bda-a7a5ad6a4077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557787} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9e9e3af-3b8c-5fe9-9bf6-926f2aefd6ba" :answer-field/key "$AB=BA={I}_{2}$" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557781} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1373a24c-5358-54bd-954f-2cee9ede5935" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186557705} {:answer/id #uuid 