 #uuid "55f9a3f4-1446-576a-9dd6-8f5cec99c326" :question/problem "<div class=\"matrix-operands\">\n<div>$O=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$R=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & -4 \\\\ -1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 8\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWhich of the following statements are true regarding the matrices $O,P,$ and $R?$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Notice that $O$ is a $3\\times 1$ column vector, $P$ is a $1\\times 2$ row vector, and $R$ is a $5\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nThere is $1$ column in $O$ and $5$ rows in $R.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $R,$ the matrices $O$ and $R$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times 1}{\\times }_{\\ne }{R}_{5\\times 2}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, there are $2$ columns in $P$ and $3$ rows in $O.$ Since the number of columns in $P$ does **not** equal the number of rows in $O,$ the matrices $P$ and $O$ are **not** conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{P}_{1\\times 2}{\\times }_{\\ne }{O}_{3\\times 1}=\\text{undefined}\n$$\n\nFinally, there is $1$ column in $O$ and $1$ row in $P.$ Since the number of columns in $O$ equals the number of rows in $P,$ the matrices $O$ and $P$ are conformable for multiplication:\n\n$$\n{O}_{3\\times \\boxed{\\text{1}}}{\\times }_{✓}{P}_{\\boxed{\\text{1}}\\times 2}=\\text{well defined}\n$$\n\nThe product $OP$ is well defined. The products $OR$ and $PO$ are undefined."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186562881 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100869 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b494140f-206a-5317-8079-ff719a253140" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Whether Two Matrices Are Conformable for Multiplication"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34dafa4d-3944-582e-bbf7-64a2dcc62647" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" 